WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:03.850
You may have thought that because Zack Snyder's
Justice League is almost here there wouldn't

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:06.220
be any more trailers coming, but you'd be
wrong.

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:10.780
On the afternoon of Sunday, March 14th, HBO
Max released a new trailer for the film formerly

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:14.410
known as the "Snyder Cut," and there's a lot
of new stuff to gawk at.

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:18.550
In particular, we see a lot more of Ray Porter's
Darkseid than we have previously, including

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:22.462
the powerful New God expressing his hunger
to rule over "all of existence."

00:00:22.462 --> 00:00:27.236
“I have turned worlds to dust.

00:00:27.236 --> 00:00:31.539
All of existence shall be mine.”

00:00:31.539 --> 00:00:35.690
But along with big, explosive moments of heroes
warring with villains and armies clashing,

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:39.360
there are a handful of small details you likely
missed upon first viewing.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.960
A number of shots in the trailer show us classic
DC Comics characters we hadn't seen before,

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:47.480
and — just like one of the most famous Justice
Leaguers — none of them are from anywhere

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:52.070
near our zip code, our hemisphere, or any
place in our particular corner of the solar

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.070
system.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:55.860
While some reports about Snyder's original
plans for Justice League claimed Darkseid

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.890
wouldn't confront the eponymous team of do-gooders
himself, a couple of moments in the trailer

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:04.010
have us wondering whether or not the ruler
of Apokolips might not be taking a much more

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:06.170
direct hand in things than previously believed.

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:11.010
Here are the small details you missed in the
(likely final) trailer for Zack Snyder's Justice

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.010
League.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:14.720
Blink and you'll miss it, but one of the most
interesting moments in the latter section

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:18.170
of the new trailer comes at around 2:03.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:22.600
Very briefly we get a shot of a woman — who
may be Diane Lane's Martha Kent, Kal-El's

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.490
adoptive mother — and her eyes are glowing
bright red.

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:29.750
Of course, even if that is Martha Kent, being
from Krypton isn't contagious so why would

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:31.280
her eyes be glowing like that?

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:35.390
The most likely answer: While that may be
Diane Lane, it isn't Martha Kent — it's

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:38.280
J'onn J'onnz, better known as the Martian
Manhunter.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:43.369
In January 2021, actor Harry Lennix confirmed
a long held fan theory that General Swanwick

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:49.030
- the character Lennix plays in both 2013's
Man of Steel and 2016's Batman v. Superman:

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:51.840
Dawn of Justice – is the Martian Manhunter
in disguise.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:55.950
At the same time, Lennix said he would finally
be revealed as J'onn J'onzz in Zack Snyder's

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:56.950
Justice League.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:01.430
The alien hero has a long list of powers in
the comics including flight, super strength,

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:04.590
telepathy, and — relevantly to this investigation
— shapeshifting.

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:09.069
It isn't a huge stretch to imagine J'onzz
taking on the form of Martha Kent.

00:02:09.069 --> 00:02:12.360
Either that, or Diane Lane's dealing with
some brutal allergies.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:16.031
Martian Manhunter isn't the only alien hero
the new trailer gives us a first look at.

00:02:16.031 --> 00:02:20.310
At around 0:57, in shots that appear to be
from the battle between the forces of Earth

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:24.140
and those of Apokolips in the distant past,
we get a glimpse of a member of the Green

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:25.140
Lantern Corps.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:27.300
who looks nothing at all like Ryan Reynolds.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:31.030
That doesn't mean he's completely unfamiliar,
however — at least not to long-time fans

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:32.030
of DC.

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:36.170
Judging by this lantern's appearance, there's
a good chance this is Yalan Gur, a Green Lantern

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:40.220
who's introduced in a flashback in 1991's
Green Lantern #19.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:44.480
Gifted with a ring that has no weaknesses,
Yalan Gur becomes overconfident and dies for

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:45.480
his error.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:48.450
Will Zack Snyder's Justice League delve significantly
into this deep canon?

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:51.849
Will we actually get to see Gur's downfall
brought to life on screen?

00:02:51.849 --> 00:02:56.180
Time will tell, but this kind of addition
would be certain to delight hardcore fans.

00:02:56.180 --> 00:03:00.840
At about 01:37 into the trailer we see something
that's never before been portrayed in live

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:03.640
action — the deadly Omega Beams of Darkseid.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:08.050
Their zig-zagging pattern is unmistakable,
and Darkseid's target may very well be Jason

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:09.360
Momoa's Aquaman.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:13.210
Whoever it is, they seem to be swimming, and
moments before this shot we get snippets from

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:16.590
the underwater battle between Aquaman and
Darkseid's lieutenant Steppenwolf.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:19.540
That may not be the last that we see of Omega
Beams, either.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:23.570
A few seconds later in the trailer, we see
red energy beams firing at the Batmobile,

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:27.360
and at around 02:07 we get more red beams
firing at Batman himself.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:30.770
It isn't clear if these last two shots emanate
from Darkseid.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:34.160
They don't share the trademark zig-zag pattern
from what we can tell, and there are plenty

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:38.460
of other possible origins in a film like Justice
League for crazy sci-fi lasers.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:41.490
Regardless, just the first shot of the Omega
Beams is intriguing.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:44.880
When Kevin Smith first started spilling the
beans on what he knew about Zack Snyder's

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:48.590
plans for Justice League, the story was that
while Darkseid would have shown up, it wouldn't

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:50.319
have been until toward the end of the film.

00:03:50.319 --> 00:03:54.020
What we see in this latest trailer could suggest
Zack Snyder's Justice League will give us

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:56.500
a Darkseid who's more involved throughout.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:59.070
Fans won't have to wait long to confirm all
this speculation.

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:04.020
Zack Snyder's Justice League will attempt
to crash the HBO Max servers on March 18th,

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:05.059
2021.

